{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on E1 question `711bd728`.\n\n1. Owners. The context requires `owners: Owners | null`, and `null`\n   states that the caller checked and no owner code exists. An\n   untyped caller that gives `undefined` is malformed input. Explore\n   throws a diagnostic `TypeError` before projection, as in item 2.\n   Add no `Lack` value. Each caller of the context is typed code in\n   this repository, so the wrong value is a programming fault, and a\n   new word in the answer would hide it. The reservation helper and\n   its equation stay unchanged.\n2. A repeated source. An exact duplicate `Source` in `assumes` is\n   malformed input, and Explore throws a diagnostic `TypeError`\n   before projection. Two versions of one key stay two sources. This\n   adds no kernel refusal and no rule for a key. Step E5 states how a\n   composition gives each step its key.\n\nOne test covers each throw.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}